From 31d1e64eb4078d31c5db445bd027f4bef0cec88b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Auchter <michael.auchter@ni.com>
Date: Fri, 7 May 2021 13:47:46 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 066/110] net: nixge: driver improvements for 6.12
 compatibility

Consolidates several nixge driver fixes and enhancements:

- Start DMA channels after request_irq to ensure IRQ handlers are
  registered before any interrupt can arrive.

- Use nixge_device_reset helper from the error IRQ handler now that
  the function purely resets the device.

- Add ethtool pause control support.

- Switch to phylink and modernize the phylink implementation:
  * Remove obsolete .validate() callback; replace with declarative
    mac_capabilities bitmask
  * Remove obsolete .mac_pcs_get_state() and .mac_an_restart() callbacks
  * Add supported_interfaces configuration (GMII and XGMII)
  * Add mac_capabilities field (10HD/FD, 100HD/FD, 1000HD/FD, 10000FD)
  * Remove phylink_config.pcs_poll field (moved to struct phylink_pcs)

- Support shared interrupts.

- Add GPIO cros-ec driver dependency which indirectly enables nixge
  loading during boot.

Signed-off-by: Michael Auchter <michael.auchter@ni.com>
Signed-off-by: Bjoern Bachmann <bjoern.bachmann@emerson.com>
